.TH SPEAKEREQ2X2 1 "January 2026" "SpeakerEQ 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
speakereq2x2 \- 2x2 stereo speaker equalization LADSPA plugin for PipeWire
.SH SYNOPSIS
Loaded via PipeWire filter-chain configuration
.br
Controlled with: \fBpw-cli\fR set-param [node-id] Props '{...}'
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBspeakereq2x2\fR is a flexible stereo speaker equalization plugin that provides:
.IP \(bu 2
2x2 stereo processing with crossbar routing
.IP \(bu 2
40 bands total: 20-band parametric EQ per channel (input and output)
.IP \(bu 2
Per-band enable/disable functionality
.IP \(bu 2
Independent delay compensation per channel
.IP \(bu 2
Comprehensive gain controls (input, output, and master)
.PP
The plugin is loaded by PipeWire as a filter-chain and integrates seamlessly with the audio pipeline. All parameters can be controlled dynamically at runtime without restarting audio services.
.SH PARAMETERS
.SS Global Controls
.TP
.B Enable
Plugin enable/disable switch (0=disabled, 1=enabled). Default: 1
.SS Input Equalizer (20 bands per channel)
.TP
.B input_<channel>_eq_<band>_type
Filter type. Range: 0-6. Default: 0 (NOOP)
.RS
.IP 0 4
NOOP - Filter disabled (passthrough)
.IP 1 4
PK - Peaking filter
.IP 2 4
LP - Lowpass filter
.IP 3 4
HP - Highpass filter
.IP 4 4
LS - Low shelf filter
.IP 5 4
HS - High shelf filter
.IP 6 4
NO - Notch filter
.RE
.TP
.B input_<channel>_eq_<band>_f
Center/corner frequency in Hz. Range: 20-20000. Default: 1000
.TP
.B input_<channel>_eq_<band>_q
Filter Q factor (bandwidth). Range: 0.1-10.0. Default: 0.707
.TP
.B input_<channel>_eq_<band>_gain
Filter gain in dB. Range: -24 to +24. Default: 0
.TP
.B input_<channel>_eq_<band>_enabled
Band enable switch (0=disabled, 1=enabled). Default: 1
.SS Crossbar Mixer
.TP
.B xbar_<in>_to_<out>
Crossbar routing coefficients. Range: 0.0-1.0. Default: Identity matrix
.br
xbar_0_to_0 = 1.0 (Left input to left output)
.br
xbar_0_to_1 = 0.0 (Left input to right output)
.br
xbar_1_to_0 = 0.0 (Right input to left output)
.br
xbar_1_to_1 = 1.0 (Right input to right output)
.SS Output Equalizer (20 bands per channel)
.TP
.B output_<channel>_eq_<band>_type
Filter type. Same values as input EQ.
.TP
.B output_<channel>_eq_<band>_f
Center/corner frequency in Hz. Range: 20-20000. Default: 1000
.TP
.B output_<channel>_eq_<band>_q
Filter Q factor. Range: 0.1-10.0. Default: 0.707
.TP
.B output_<channel>_eq_<band>_gain
Filter gain in dB. Range: -24 to +24. Default: 0
.TP
.B output_<channel>_eq_<band>_enabled
Band enable switch (0=disabled, 1=enabled). Default: 1
.SS Delay Compensation
.TP
.B delay_<channel>_ms
Per-channel delay in milliseconds. Range: 0-100. Default: 0
.SS Gain Controls
.TP
.B input_gain_<channel>_db
Input gain per channel in dB. Range: -100 to +24. Default: 0
.TP
.B output_gain_<channel>_db
Output gain per channel in dB. Range: -100 to +24. Default: 0
.TP
.B master_gain_db
Master gain applied to all channels. Range: -100 to +24. Default: 0
.SH PARAMETER CONTROL
All parameters can be controlled dynamically using the \fBpw-cli\fR command:
.SS Find the node ID
.nf
NODE_ID=$(pw-cli list-objects | grep -B 10 "Speaker EQ 2x2" | grep "id:" | head -1 | awk '{print $2}' | tr -d ',')
.fi
.SS View current parameters
.nf
pw-cli enum-params $NODE_ID Props
.fi
.SS Set a parameter value
.nf
pw-cli set-param $NODE_ID Props '{ "parameter_name": value }'
.fi
.SS Set multiple parameters at once
.nf
pw-cli set-param $NODE_ID Props '{
    "parameter1": value1,
    "parameter2": value2
}'
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Find the node and view parameters
.nf
NODE_ID=$(pw-cli list-objects | grep -B 10 "Speaker EQ 2x2" | grep "id:" | head -1 | awk '{print $2}' | tr -d ',')
pw-cli enum-params $NODE_ID Props
.fi
.SS Add a 3dB boost at 80Hz on left output channel, band 1
.nf
pw-cli set-param $NODE_ID Props '{ "output_0_eq_1_type": 1 }'
pw-cli set-param $NODE_ID Props '{ "output_0_eq_1_f": 80.0 }'
pw-cli set-param $NODE_ID Props '{ "output_0_eq_1_q": 1.0 }'
pw-cli set-param $NODE_ID Props '{ "output_0_eq_1_gain": 3.0 }'
.fi
.SS Add a highpass filter at 30Hz on both input channels
.nf
pw-cli set-param $NODE_ID Props '{ "input_0_eq_1_type": 3 }'
pw-cli set-param $NODE_ID Props '{ "input_0_eq_1_f": 30.0 }'
pw-cli set-param $NODE_ID Props '{ "input_0_eq_1_q": 0.707 }'
pw-cli set-param $NODE_ID Props '{ "input_1_eq_1_type": 3 }'
pw-cli set-param $NODE_ID Props '{ "input_1_eq_1_f": 30.0 }'
pw-cli set-param $NODE_ID Props '{ "input_1_eq_1_q": 0.707 }'
.fi
.SS Add 5ms delay to left channel for alignment
.nf
pw-cli set-param $NODE_ID Props '{ "delay_0_ms": 5.0 }'
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/local/lib/ladspa/speakereq2x2.so
LADSPA plugin library
.TP
.B /etc/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d/90-speakereq.conf
PipeWire filter-chain configuration (system-wide)
.TP
.B ~/.config/pipewire/pipewire.conf.d/90-speakereq.conf
PipeWire filter-chain configuration (user-specific)
.SH CHANNEL NUMBERING
Channels are zero-indexed:
.IP \(bu 2
Channel 0 = Left
.IP \(bu 2
Channel 1 = Right
.PP
EQ bands are numbered 1-20 for each channel.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Parameter changes take effect immediately without restarting audio.
.IP \(bu 2
The crossbar mixer allows routing flexibility (e.g., swapping channels or creating mono from stereo).
